    "intro_html":  "Giouvetsi is what happens when a Greek cook decides the pasta should cook in the meat sauce instead of a separate pot of boiling water. Orzo goes into the pan near the end and swells up on tomato, cinnamon, and nutmeg while the turkey finishes around it. Parmesan on top, straight from oven to containers. Each one carries \u003cstrong\u003e{{cal}} calories and {{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
